=====================================
       DOOR TRANSVERSAL GUIDE
=====================================


::QUICK REFERENCES::
-------------------------------------


Door Types (# (type, open/closed)):
0 (no door, closed)
1 (no-door, open)
2 (door, open)
3 (rope/hole/ladder, open)
4 (non-interactive door, closed)
5 (waypoint, waypoint)


Key:
**no door ==> a door cannot be used**
**door ==> a door will be used**
**rope ==> a rope will be used**
**hole ==> a hole will be used**
**ladder ==> a ladder will be used**
**hole-in-ground ==> hole pieces in map (desginated ground piece)**
**rope/hole/ladder ==> a rope, hole, hole-in-ground, ladder may be used**
**non-interactive door ==> a door will be used (may be a special looking door; will be inactive when not in use)**
**open ==> user can interact to use**
**closed ==> user doesn't directly interact to use**
**waypoint ==> user must interact with a side to use**

-------------------------------------


Transversal Array (explained):
---- => TOP,RIGHT,BOTTOM,LEFT {map edge doorways}
--- => INNER-LEFT,INNER-CENTER,INNER-RIGHT {inner map pathways}
------- ==> T,R,B,L,IL,IC,IR {full transversal array}


Allowed Transversal {EXIT -> ENTER}:
X------ -> --X-XXX
-X----- -> ---XXXX
--X---- -> X---XXX
---X--- -> -X--XXX
----X-- -> XXXXXXX
-----X- -> XXXXXXX
------X -> XXXXXXX


Allowed Door-Pass {DOOR EXIT(DOOR ENTER,...,DOOR ENTER)}:
0(N/A,5,4); 1(1,3,0,4,5); 2(1,2,4,5); 3(1,3,0,4,5); 4(1,2,3,0,4,5); 5(0,5,4,1,2,3)

-------------------------------------


